  "ref": "LUK.24.44",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected s020, s021 and s022: the accepted alignment gave all things to πάντα under rule 17's generic-noun clause and a bare which to the article under rule 90. Rule 90 is scoped in terms to where the ASV writes only one English word for the article-plus-participle pair, and here it writes things, which and are written, so that rule does not reach this unit.",
    "Rule 80's closing clause settles the shape — πᾶς ὁ ἔχων → every / one / that hath — and rule 102 scopes rule 17's generic-noun clause to anarthrous Greek, so with τά expressed the supplied things is the article's. LUK.24.14 reads the identical πάντων τῶν συμβεβηκότων this way, and LUK.24.12 and LUK.24.18 both leave the relativizer on the participle.",
    "Reading all things as one unit on the quantifier remains defensible where no article stands, as LUK.24.9's ταῦτα πάντα → all these things shows; what decides it here is the expressed article, which is the test rules 51, 58 and 102 already use.",
    "Nothing else in the verse is changed: the token partition, the rule 68 copula on Οὗτοι, the rule 20 empty article and the rule 51 determiners on προφήταις and ψαλμοῖς stand as accepted."
  ]
